# Archived solo-mode template. Rename back to .yml only when OpenLife returns
# to issue-driven LifeModel-HS tracking.
name: LifeModel-HS Epic
description: Track the full LifeModel-HS MVP phase.
title: "Epic: LifeModel-HS MVP"
labels:
  - lifemodel-hs
  - mvp
  - epic
  - governance
body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        Use this template for the top-level LifeModel-HS MVP tracking issue.

        Required references:
        - `plans/lifemodel_hs_mvp_task_specs.md`
        - `plans/adr/0013-lifemodel-hs-source-of-truth-governance.md`
        - `plans/lifemodel_hs_architecture_plan.md`

  - type: textarea
    id: goal
    attributes:
      label: Goal
      description: State the phase goal in one or two paragraphs.
      value: |
        Implement the LifeModel-HS MVP according to:

        - `plans/lifemodel_hs_mvp_task_specs.md`
        - `plans/adr/0013-lifemodel-hs-source-of-truth-governance.md`
        - `plans/lifemodel_hs_architecture_plan.md`

        LifeModel-HS should move OpenLife from a mostly static YAML/profile LifeModel toward an additive, local-first, user-governed Personal Heuristic System.
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: mvp_definition
    attributes:
      label: MVP Definition
      description: Define what makes the MVP real, not just structurally present.
      value: |
        The MVP proves that LifeModel-HS can influence real Agent behavior through accepted, governed, metadata-safe HS assets without replacing the current YAML LifeModel source path.

        The MVP is not complete because stores exist. It is complete only when selected policies/heuristics can affect narrow runtime behavior, be audited, be regression-checked, and remain proposal-first for risky changes.
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: architecture_invariants
    attributes:
      label: Architecture Invariants
      description: These invariants should not be violated by task PRs.
      value: |
        - Current YAML LifeModel remains a compatibility materialized view.
        - Accepted HS assets are the long-term target source of truth, but migration is phased.
        - Privacy is hard Policy, not soft Heuristic.
        - Heuristics cannot relax Policy.
        - Raw Life Data cannot directly mutate canonical HS assets.
        - Risky HS mutation is Proposal-first.
        - High-risk identity, values, long-term goals, sensitive relationships, and privacy boundaries require explicit user confirmation.
        - Runtime selection audit must be metadata-safe.
        - Deterministic regression comes before broad runtime integration.
        - Existing PromptStack, ModelRouter, ToolRuntime, ExecutionFacade, Proposal, and AgentRunEvent governance must remain intact.
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: review_policy
    attributes:
      label: Review Policy
      description: Define what each task PR must prove and what reviewers should reject.
      value: |
        Each task PR must include:

        - Summary of changed files.
        - Explanation of how the change follows ADR 0013.
        - Tests run and results.
        - Any out-of-scope work intentionally avoided.
        - Remaining risks or follow-ups.

        Review should reject PRs that:

        - broaden runtime authority without an accepted ADR,
        - bypass Proposal-first governance,
        - store raw sensitive data unnecessarily,
        - relax privacy policy through heuristics,
        - switch LifeModel source of truth in one step,
        - implement adjacent LMHS tasks without explicit scope.
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: task_issues
    attributes:
      label: Task Issues
      description: Link each child issue as it is created.
      value: |
        - [ ] LMHS-1: EvidenceStore MVP Skeleton
        - [ ] LMHS-2: HeuristicStore MVP Skeleton
        - [ ] LMHS-3: Policy/Heuristic Boundary And Built-In MVP Assets
        - [ ] LMHS-4: ContextSelector And HeuristicSelector MVP
        - [ ] LMHS-5: Deterministic RegressionSuite MVP
        - [ ] LMHS-6: Runtime Integration MVP
        - [ ] LMHS-7: Negative Evidence Loop MVP
        - [ ] LMHS-8: Materialized YAML Compatibility View MVP
        - [ ] LMHS-9: Minimal Review And Trace Surface
        - [ ] LMHS-10: Legacy Evolution Path Audit
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: exit_criteria
    attributes:
      label: Exit Criteria
      value: |
        - EvidenceStore and HeuristicStore exist with focused tests.
        - Privacy-sensitive LocalOnly policy is enforced as hard policy.
        - External write actions remain draft/proposal-first.
        - Low-energy planning changes runtime guidance in a bounded, testable way.
        - Rejected reminder behavior creates negative evidence and affects similar future reminders narrowly.
        - ContextSelector and HeuristicSelector select assets by task, privacy, risk, lifecycle, and budget without injecting the whole HS.
        - Runtime selection audit is metadata-safe and inspectable.
        - RegressionSuite has deterministic checks for the MVP behaviors.
        - YAML remains a compatibility materialized view and does not contain raw HS internals.
        - No high-risk identity, value, mission, long-term goal, sensitive relationship, or privacy-boundary update can auto-apply.
        - Legacy write-path audit exists and does not reveal newly introduced hidden high-risk direct writes.
        - `make ci` passes.
    validations:
      required: true
